       title="JirAI: What's new" id="JirAI-Whats-New">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Highlights of each JirAI release, newest first.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Highlights of each JirAI release, newest first.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Release highlights of JirAI, the Jira Cloud plugin for JetBrains IDEs, newest release first.</web-summary>

    <p>This page lists the user-visible changes in each JirAI release, newest first.</p>
    <p>The full change log is on the <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/33954-jirai/versions">JetBrains Marketplace versions page</a>.</p>

    <timeline>
        <item title="2026.3.34">
            <p>Virtual boards linked to Jira, with Jira changes you approve on the board.</p>
        </item>
        <item title="2026.3.33">
            <p>Agent skills for Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and Junie.</p>
        </item>
        <item title="2026.3.30 to 2026.3.32">
            <p>The virtual board, Go To, starred boards and team-managed boards.</p>
        </item>
        <item title="2026.3.24 to 2026.3.29">
            <p>The Backlog tab, Create Branch from another branch or a tag, and fixes.</p>
        </item>
    </timeline>

    <chapter title="2026.3.34" id="release-2026-3-34">
        <list>
            <li>
                <p>A virtual board started on a Jira parent shows its children as cards with their live Jira status, in <control>To Do</control>, <control>In Progress</control>, <control>Ready to merge</control> and <control>Done</control>.
                    Done is never automatic: <control>Move to Done…</control> is on the cards, and <control>Create in Jira…</control> turns a local phase into a child.
                    See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="jira-linked-board">A board linked to Jira</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li><p>Approve or reject each Jira change the agent asks for, right on the board. The new agent tools <code>jirai_start_jira_issue</code> and <code>jirai_add_jira_comment</code> only queue a change.
                See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="approve-jira-changes">Approve the agent's Jira changes</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Send notes to the newest session</control> hands the board's notes to the agent chat that called it most recently. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="newest-session">Send notes to the newest session</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Reopen a closed board from the <control>JirAI</control> tool window title bar. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="reopen-board">Reopen a closed board</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>A new agent skill, <code>/work-on-jira-issue</code>. See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Skills.topic">Agent skills</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Every JirAI settings page shows the JirAI icon.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.33" id="release-2026-3-33">
        <list>
            <li><p>JirAI offers once to add the <code>/use-virtual-board</code> and <code>/jira-ticket</code> skills to Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and Junie.
                Add, update or remove them later in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | JirAI | Agent Skills</ui-path> or from <ui-path>Tools | Add JirAI Skills to AI Agents…</ui-path>.
                See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Skills.topic">Agent skills</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Virtual board fixes: a card whose plan file is missing says <control>Plan file not found</control>, a finished phase clears its "now doing" text, and the board no longer overrides a stage the agent set.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.32" id="release-2026-3-32">
        <list>
            <li><p>Agent work boards are now the virtual board. Its four agent tools are always listed; if you had turned the old ones off, check <ui-path>Settings | AI | MCP Server | Exposed Tools</ui-path> again.</p></li>
            <li><p>An opened card shows what the phase is about, when it last changed and how long it was in progress, and fills an empty what, steps and files from the plan file.</p></li>
            <li><p>A card in progress with no update for 20 minutes shows <control>No update for N min</control>. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="read-board">Read the board</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Refresh</control> asks the agent's main session to update the board, with a <control>Copy</control> fallback. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="refresh">Refresh and ask for an update</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Notes go to the agent session that started the board; the <control>Send to</control> choice is gone. Plan and spec files can live outside the open project.</p></li>
            <li><p>Go To highlights the item you jump to for a moment.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.31" id="release-2026-3-31">
        <list>
            <li><p>Leave a note on a phase for your AI agent and read its reply on the card. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="notes">Notes to the agent</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Color a phase card from its menu to group related phases, and switch to the <control>Graph</control> view to see how phases depend on each other. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic" anchor="graph-view">Graph view</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>The steps count is colored by real progress and falls back to the plan's ticked checkboxes.</p></li>
            <li><p>Go To greys out an item with nowhere to go and says why.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.30" id="release-2026-3-30">
        <list>
            <li><p>Ask your AI agent for a JirAI work board, and it shows its plan as live phase cards in an editor tab. See <a href="JirAI-Virtual-Board.topic">Virtual board</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Go To: from any work item, jump to its card on the <control>Board</control>, its row on the <control>Backlog</control> or the <control>List</control>, or its parent and linked items. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="go-to">Go to a work item's card or row</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Star a board in the board picker to list it first. Until you pick a board, the <control>Board</control> and <control>Backlog</control> tabs open on the board you most recently viewed in Jira, and only a board you pick is remembered. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="open-board">Open a board</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Team-managed boards open in the <control>Board</control> tab, with drag-and-drop. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="team-managed-boards">Team-managed boards</a>.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.29" id="release-2026-3-29">
        <list>
            <li><p>Collapsible <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> sections in Create and AI drafts keep their text.</p></li>
            <li><p>Checking out a branch that was deleted meanwhile says the branch no longer exists.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.27 and 2026.3.28" id="release-2026-3-27">
        <list>
            <li><p>JirAI needs a 2026.3 IDE from build 263.6800 on. See <a href="JirAI-Installation.topic" anchor="requirements">Requirements</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>When Jira no longer accepts your API token, JirAI says you are not signed in instead of showing an empty list, and a new token takes effect at once.</p></li>
            <li><p>The draft check of the agent tools rejects labels with a space and texts over Jira's length limits, and names the values it could not check.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.26" id="release-2026-3-26">
        <list>
            <li><p>JirAI's buttons and shortcuts work while the IDE is indexing.</p></li>
            <li><p>The issue list updates by itself a few seconds after you change or create an issue in JirAI.</p></li>
            <li><p>Signing in or out in one project window updates every open project window.</p></li>
            <li><p>With several projects open, the agent tools no longer fail with "Unable to determine the target project".</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.25" id="release-2026-3-25">
        <p>The issue timeline, the <control>Breakdown</control> and the space tabs open again on IDE builds 263.6800 and later. Fixes for the <control>Backlog</control> and the <control>Board</control>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.24" id="release-2026-3-24">
        <list>
            <li><p>The <control>Backlog</control> tab shows a Scrum board's active and future sprints and its backlog. Move a work item to a sprint or the backlog, or reorder it, from its menu or by dragging. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="backlog-tab">Backlog tab</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Create Branch</control> can start from another branch or a tag: select <control>Start from</control> in the dialog.</p></li>
            <li><p>When uncommitted changes clash, Create Branch and Check Out offer <control>Smart Checkout</control> or <control>Don't Checkout</control>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Maximize</control> on a Summary or Reports widget opens it large over the page.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.23" id="release-2026-3-23">
        <list>
            <li><p>Open a card's work item in the IDE from the board with a double-click, <shortcut>Enter</shortcut> or <control>Open</control>. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="open-card-issue">Open a card's work item in the IDE</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>When you drag or reorder a card, the board no longer offers positions next to sub-tasks that Jira cannot keep, and a card dragged to another column lands where Jira places it.</p></li>
            <li><p>Every person filter and picker lists you first, under <control>Unassigned</control>, and opens on the current value.</p></li>
            <li><p>Editing a comment or the description shows <control>Cancel</control> and a highlighted <control>Save</control> on the right.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.22" id="release-2026-3-22">
        <list>
            <li><p>The <control>Breakdown</control> tab has a filter bar (search, status, type, priority, assignee, reporter, unresolved and sort) and <control>Show Hierarchy</control> with <control>Expand All</control> and <control>Collapse All</control>.
                See <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic" anchor="breakdown-filters">Filter the breakdown</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Copy Issue URL</control> is in every issue menu. The Timeline and details menus also gain <control>Open in Jira</control> and <control>Copy Issue Key</control>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Work item types that cannot have child work items open with only the <control>Timeline</control> tab.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.21" id="release-2026-3-21">
        <p>JirAI is free: no licence, trial or subscription is needed to install and use it. See <a href="JirAI-Installation.topic"/>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.20" id="release-2026-3-20">
        <p>Edit your comments from the issue Timeline. Text and formatting are editable; mentions, images, tables and anything else the editor cannot show stay as locked pieces and are kept exactly as they are.
            Restricted and service-desk comments still open in Jira. See <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic" anchor="edit-comment">Edit a comment</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.19" id="release-2026-3-19">
        <list>
            <li><p>The <control>Summary</control> tab of a space matches Jira's Summary: four tiles (completed, updated and created in the range, and due soon in the next 7 days) and six widgets, each of which can show its table.
                Hide a widget from its menu and bring it back from <control>Hidden widgets</control>. See <a href="JirAI-Metrics.topic" anchor="summary-tab">Summary tab</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>New space filters: <control>Status</control>, <control>Priority</control>, <control>Parent</control>, <control>Created</control>, <control>Updated</control> and <control>Due date</control> on Summary and Reports;
                Summary also offers <control>Sprint</control>, <control>Fix version</control>, <control>Component</control> and <control>Label</control>. Throughput, Created vs completed and Work in progress by age are on Reports.</p></li>
            <li><p>Drag a card to another column or to a new place in its column. Jira's transition chooser and screens appear as they do from the card menu. See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" anchor="move-card">Move a card</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Create Branch</control> from an issue opens the IDE's New Branch dialog with a name such as <code>PFX-42-fix-login-timeout</code>, then offers to move the issue to In Progress.
                See <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" anchor="create-branch">Create a branch from an issue</a> and <a href="JirAI-Settings-Reference.topic" anchor="settings-development">Development settings</a>.</p></li>
            <li><p>The status bar shows the issue of your current Git branch, with <control>Open Current Jira Issue</control>. See <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" anchor="current-issue-status-bar"/>.</p></li>
            <li><p>With changelists on, an empty commit message starts with the current issue's key. Drafts and Git commit templates are never overwritten. See <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" anchor="commit-message-issue-key"/>.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.18" id="release-2026-3-18">
        <list>
            <li><p>The Lead time and Cycle time tiles moved off the <control>Summary</control> tab; both are on <control>Reports</control>.</p></li>
            <li><p>The agent tools tell your AI assistant to check with JirAI before it creates an issue, and a failed check says what to do next. See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic" anchor="agent-tool-errors">When a tool call fails</a>.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.17" id="release-2026-3-17">
        <list>
            <li><p><control>Push to Jira</control> is available from a right-click on a Markdown file in the Project view. It is not offered under Remote Development. See <a href="JirAI-AI-Workflows.topic" anchor="push-to-jira"/>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Deleting an attachment warns you when the attachment is shown inline in a comment.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.16" id="release-2026-3-16">
        <list>
            <li>
                <p>The <control>Board</control> tab of a space shows a company-managed Kanban board, or the active sprint of a Scrum board, with columns, cards, WIP limits, quick filters and an <control>Assignee</control> filter.</p>
                <p>JirAI remembers the board you picked for each space.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Move a card to another column, or up and down within its column, from the card menu: the <control>More</control> button, a right-click or <shortcut>Shift+Enter</shortcut>.</p>
                <p>When Jira needs fields for the transition, its transition screen opens.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>The board works from the keyboard: <shortcut>Tab</shortcut> moves between columns and the arrow keys move between cards.</p>
                <p>A screen reader announces each card and column.</p>
            </li>
        </list>
        <img src="jirai_board_kanban.png" alt="Kanban board tab of a space with columns, cards and a column over its WIP limit" width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
        <p>See <a href="JirAI-Board.topic">Board</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.15" id="release-2026-3-15">
        <list>
            <li>
                <p>A house standard tells JirAI what your team expects on an issue beyond Jira's required fields: fields that must be set, headings the description must have and patterns a value must match.</p>
                <p>An AI assistant that validates a draft is told when the draft misses one of these rules.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic">Agent tools and house standard</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li><p>A one-time notification points you to the IDE's MCP server setting when the server is off, so that the JirAI agent tools become visible to your assistant.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Open ↗</control> beside the <control>Parent</control> field opens the parent work item, and the <control>Breakdown</control> tab links to the parent.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Add child</control> flags issue types that cannot sit under the parent, picks the type when only one fits and tells you when you cannot create in the parent's project.</p></li>
            <li><p>Fixes for the <control>Breakdown</control> list and the <control>List</control> tab of a space: the list keeps its position and selection when you fold, edit or refresh.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.14" id="release-2026-3-14">
        <list>
            <li>
                <p>The <control>Breakdown</control> section in the issue details and the <control>Breakdown</control> tab beside the issue timeline list an issue's child work items, with <control>Add child</control>.</p>
                <p>See <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic">Timeline and breakdown</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li><p>The <control>List</control> tab of a space shows work items under their parent as a foldable tree, with <control>Show Hierarchy</control>, <control>Expand All</control> and <control>Collapse All</control>.</p></li>
            <li><p>Right-click the issue details and choose <control>Hide Fields…</control> to hide several custom fields at once.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <control>Type</control> row in the issue details shows the issue type icon.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <control>Push to Jira</control> dialog shows its warnings box only when there are warnings.</p></li>
        </list>
        <!-- planned-image src="jirai_breakdown_tab.png" alt="Breakdown tab of an epic listing its child work items with the parent link and Add child" -->
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.12 and 2026.3.13" id="release-2026-3-12">
        <list>
            <li><p>The <control>Project</control> and <control>Issue type</control> pickers on the Create form show project avatars and issue type icons.</p></li>
            <li><p>Agent tools: an AI coding assistant connected to the IDE's MCP server can ask JirAI for a Jira project's real create screen and check a drafted issue against it before filing it.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.13 is a maintenance release with no visible changes.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.11" id="release-2026-3-11">
        <list>
            <li><p>Sign in and sign out from <ui-path>Settings | Tools | JirAI</ui-path>, in addition to the tool window.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <control>Sprint</control> filter of space reports lists all sprints when a space has several boards.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.5 to 2026.3.10" id="recent-improvements">
        <list>
            <li><p>2026.3.10: hide a custom field from the eye icon on its row, and manage hidden fields in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | JirAI | Field Visibility</ui-path>.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.9: Markdown in the Create form description, <control>Push to Jira</control> for Markdown documents, document presets for Superpowers and spec-kit, and the <control>List</control> tab of a space.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.8: switching between a space's tabs no longer loads the space again.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.7: exclude a filter value with a second click or <shortcut>Shift</shortcut>+click, <control>All</control> and <control>Clear</control> in every filter popup, and several people in the <control>Assignee</control> and <control>Reporter</control> filters.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.6: filter space reports by sprint, sprint status, fix version, component and label.</p></li>
            <li><p>2026.3.5: space pages with the <control>Summary</control> and <control>Reports</control> tabs, and the large-space setting in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | JirAI | Metrics</ui-path>.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="2026.3.1 to 2026.3.4" id="jirai-core-experience">
        <p>The first releases brought the core of JirAI:</p>
        <list>
            <li><p>The <control>JirAI</control> tool window with quick filters, filter chips, search and sorting.</p></li>
            <li><p>A Create form built from your project's own create screen.</p></li>
            <li><p>Issue details with in-place editing, workflow transitions, attachments and issue links.</p></li>
            <li><p>The issue timeline with comments, <code>@mentions</code> and description editing.</p></li>
            <li><p>Support for Remote Development, corporate HTTP proxies and the IDE credential store.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

